CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 07:42:41 2026 -0500

    Announce the Sidekiq push at boot and recognize queue_adapter :sidekiq in the ledger
    
    Now that perform_later pushes to Redis under :sidekiq, the boot line
    that says where jobs go is true, and the initializer ledger can count
    config.active_job.queue_adapter = :sidekiq as honored instead of
    dropped. Both were held back from #901 until this wiring existed.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <[redacted-email]>

diff --git a/runtime/spinel/scaffold/main.rb b/runtime/spinel/scaffold/main.rb
index ca7025438..376369da1 100644
--- a/runtime/spinel/scaffold/main.rb
+++ b/runtime/spinel/scaffold/main.rb
@@ -878,6 +878,8 @@ Broadcasts.set_transport(Cable::Transport.new)
 # reaches this line keeps the inline behaviour rather than dropping work
 # into an Array nobody reads.
 ActiveJob.register_drain
+# Under queue_adapter :sidekiq jobs go to Redis instead; say where.
+SidekiqPush.announce if JobRegistry.sidekiq?
 Thread.new do
   Main.job_loop
 end
diff --git a/runtime/spinel/scaffold/ruby_overlay/config.ru b/runtime/spinel/scaffold/ruby_overlay/config.ru
index f3d66389c..4f57f74b7 100644
--- a/runtime/spinel/scaffold/ruby_overlay/config.ru
+++ b/runtime/spinel/scaffold/ruby_overlay/config.ru
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ Db.checkpoint_in_background!
 # thread in each serving process instead of running it inside the
 # request (ActiveJob.drain_in_background!).
 ActiveJob.drain_in_background!
+# Under queue_adapter :sidekiq jobs go to Redis instead; say where.
+SidekiqPush.announce if JobRegistry.sidekiq?
 
 # Register the Cable registry as the broadcasts transport: every
 # `Broadcasts.record` call from model callbacks now also fans out
